      "writtenOn": "2022-08-03T17:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Thanks for writing tests. Try setting CQ+1 to see what your incremental test coverage is.\n2. It looks like you\u0027re substantially replicating the power button state machine within the DPM, such that you\u0027re reproducing some of the power button time limits outside the DPM. This might be too involved to be worth it, but would it make sense to have the DPM directly simulate both press and release events and then have the power button code handle everything else?",
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2546bf73_dbcbdb24",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T19:57:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is some replication here that we could potentially avoid by just adding simulated press and release functions to the power button API and calling them on press/release alert from the USB PD partner. But, I don\u0027t think we should directly simulate both press and release events. And, I\u0027ve avoided that type of implementation because it would lead to bad behavior with some docks.\n\nThe particular dock I am testing with (HP Thunderbolt G4) will send only a press event on short button taps (violating the PD spec), but will send press then release events on a longer sustained press. If we entirely use the power button state machine and a dock just sends a press event, we would interpret this as a power button hold and shutdown the device.\n\nTo be a bit safer, this implementation will only act on a power button release after checking that the press-\u003erelease events are within a valid time frame. Basically, having this in the DPM allows us to filter out bad behavior from docks which the power button state machine can\u0027t handle.",
      "parentUuid": "50c2e979_02556a44",
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
