      "writtenOn": "2022-08-03T17:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I vaguely get what you\u0027re trying to do here, but I find this math hard to follow. The mechanic of checking the remaining time on a timer for an event that has already happened is unconventional. Elsewhere in the PD stack, we would deal with this by disabling the old timer and setting a new timer. This also seems to depend on how soon the DPM runs again after the button is released in a way that I don\u0027t feel like I understand, because the timer is still running.\n\nCan you clarify this, ideally in the form of simplified code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 575,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 579,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
