      "writtenOn": "2022-08-04T22:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like we could store the time the power button was depressed based on the release time?  I also wonder if the release transition could continue straight into the `DPM_PD_BUTTON_RELEASED` case to reduce the latency between receiving the release and acting on the power button. Or I suppose that would imply the released state itself is unnecessary, and could instead process and then return to idle.",
      "parentUuid": "7d69881c_347524b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 575,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 579,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd566a39_5dfa82d7",
