      "lineNbr": 579,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T20:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I think I better understand what the CL is trying to do now. Here is an approach that I think would be more idiomatic in our codebase:\n1. Have a new named timer like `DPM_TIMER_PD_BUTTON_SHORT_PRESS`. It might make sense to rename `DPM_TIMER_PD_BUTTON_PRESS` to avoid ambiguity.\n2. When we get a press event, start the timer with timeout `CONFIG_USB_PD_SHORT_PRESS_MAX_MS * MSEC`.\n3. When we get a release event, check if the timer is expired. If it isn\u0027t, treat the press as a short press. If it is, treat it as a long press.\n4. When we get a release event, or when the maximum release timer expires, stop the short press timer.\n\nI don\u0027t think you need to directly deal with or store the current time.",
      "parentUuid": "0d721f63_22648a47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 575,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 579,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
