        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T19:57:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t really the minimum press time. Any press followed by a release under the long press time limit will be considered a press. This is the duration of a simulated press after DPM detects a short press. For example if I press a USB PD power button for 3 seconds, the DPM will then simulate a 500ms power button press. It\u0027s similar to running `powerbtn 500` from the ec console. This config can change how long the simulate power button press is. It only needs to be long enough to bring up the Shutdown/Sign Out/Lock UI.\n\nThe reason I put it here instead of adding it as a config is because it\u0027s not something that will impact how we treat different button presses like CONFIG_USB_PD_SHORT_PRESS_MAX_MS or CONFIG_USB_PD_LONG_PRESS_MAX_MS. If this type of constant should be defined somewhere else, let me know.",
      "parentUuid": "54db247c_e2311945",
      "revId": "31178b403129f28c84e3c59adfbefe4f1ebaa5b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
